Subject: [PATCH] feat: butterfly and moth netting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Butterflies and moths could not be caught.

Change. Catching butterflies and moths: a wielded butterfly net or
magic butterfly net, or barehanded at 10 levels above the requirement;
the OSRS 256 roll with the wiki's skilling success charts (black
warlock, sunlight and moonlight moths; the other butterflies copy the
black warlock). A butterfly jar keeps the catch; without one it is
released and its effect applies. Jarred butterflies get their Release op
(Attack/Defence/Strength boosts, Hitpoints, the sunlight moth's restore,
the moonlight moth's prayer). The sunlight moth restores drained stats
except Prayer and, as in OSRS, not Sailing; caught without a jar it also
restores 5% run energy (the jarred moth does not). Data in the
server-only dbtable hunter_butterflies (56012, rows 60281-60287), own
ButterflyPluginPack. Needs the Hunter module skeleton PR.

Tests. Integration suite ButterflyScriptTest (6): a jar is swapped for
exactly one butterfly, a jarless catch applies the boost, a jarless
sunlight moth restores 5% run energy, a jarred sunlight moth restores
drained stats but not Sailing or run energy, Release gives the jar back
once, barehanded below ten extra levels always fails.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Ruby harvest, Sapphire glacialis, Snowy knight,
Black warlock (and its item page), Sunlight Moth (effects, run energy,
the Sailing bug note), Moonlight moth (levels, XP, effects, success
charts); cache item ops (Release).

Caveats. Guesses: the ruby harvest, sapphire glacialis and snowy knight
curves (no chart; the black warlock's), one 2-tick swing per click, the
barehanded animation, the 7-tick respawn, the messages, failing silently
below the level, which moonlight moth variants are catchable. Not done:
sharing effects in multicombat, butterfly mixes.

